#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054446 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/id #uuid "a138e1a7-52c5-5763-975e-cab082266099" :question/math-academy-id "e-13199" :question/problem "Find $\\mathcal{P}(A)$ if $A = \\{ 2, 4, \\{ 8 \\} \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $A,$ denoted $\\mathcal{P}(A),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $A,$ including the empty set $\\emptyset.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $A$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](images/b3/b3af256806e0aeb0396564320800f908c66d5830ab46e676dfc51ceab24154f6.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $A$ are\n\n$$\n\\emptyset = \\{\\},\\quad \\{2\\},\\quad \\{4\\},\\quad \\{ \\{8\\} \\}, \\quad \\{2, 4\\},\\quad \\{2, \\{8\\}\\},\\quad \\{4, \\{8\\}\\},\\quad\\{2, 4, \\{8\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{P}(A) = \\{\\emptyset, \\{2\\}, \\{4\\}, \\{\\{8\\}\\}, \\{2, 4\\}, \\{2, \\{8\\}\\}, \\{4, \\{8\\}\\},\\{2, 4, \\{8\\}\\}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054447 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e22a7b0-753b-51b1-8946-5d17456aa778" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Power Set"}] :question/id #uuid "a72a78b7-eaef-59a3-a23a-82d291e8253a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13200" :question/problem "If $Y = \\{ 1, \\{ 3, 5 \\}, 7, X \\},$ then what is $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(Y)\\right|?$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $Y,$ we have $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(Y)\\right| = 2^{\\left| Y \\right|}.$\n\nIn this case, $\\left| Y \\right| = 4,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\left| \\mathcal{P}(Y) \\right| = 2^{\\left| Y \\right|} = 2^{4} = 16.\n$$\n\nRemember that $\\{ 3,5 \\}$ is a single element in the set $Y.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054448 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/id #uuid "b8db07f6-cdbf-5d00-8f3c-6f8b07277ac3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13201" :question/problem "Given that $Y =\\{\\mu\\}$ and $Z =\\{1,2\\},$ find $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(\\mathcal{P}(Y\\times Z))\\right|.$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S,$ we have $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(S)\\right| = 2^{\\left| S \\right|}.$ Also, $|S \\times T| = |S| \\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\left| Y \\right| = 1, \\qquad\n\\left| Z \\right| = 2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Y\\times Z)| & ={2}^{|Y\\times Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|Y|\\,\\cdot \\,|Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1\\cdot 2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(Y\\times Z))| & ={2}^{|P(Y\\times Z)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054449 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "ceb40e91-12d8-5636-8b98-fa41aaca33b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13214" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathcal{P}(\\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\})  = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\} \\}$\n\nII. $\\mathcal{P} (\\{ \\emptyset, \\{0\\} \\} ) = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{0\\}, \\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\}, \\{0, \\emptyset\\} \\}$\n\nIII. $\\mathcal{P}( \\mathcal{P}(\\{y\\}))  = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}, \\{\\{y\\}\\}, \\{\\emptyset, \\{y\\}\\} \\}$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $\\mathcal{P}(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $\\emptyset.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $\\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\}.$ So, its power set must be $\\{ \\emptyset, \\{\\{\\emptyset\\}\\} \\}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set $\\{ \\emptyset, \\{0\\} \\} .$ So, its power set must be $\\{ \\emptyset, \\{\\{0\\}\\}, \\{\\emptyset\\}, \\{\\emptyset, \\{0\\} \\} \\}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that we are given the set $\\{y\\}.$ So, its power set must be $\\{\\emptyset, \\{y\\} \\}.$ Therefore, $\\mathcal{P}( \\mathcal{P}(\\{y\\})) = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}, \\{\\{y\\}\\}, \\{\\emptyset, \\{y\\}\\} \\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0392591f-5068-5700-a5bc-4d271db178a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{x\\},\\{n\\},\\{x,y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494324} {:answer/id #uuid "b10ff497-27d6-5108-adb4-5fa60e2cf4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{x,y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494731} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd24002-3393-5c3f-be05-4886caf51bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{x,y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494759} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5be63a-fb4b-57d1-997b-57d44ca45c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{x\\},\\{y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494809} {:answer/id #uuid "e74e2092-2925-569e-886c-80bc60ca20d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{x,y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e74e2092-2925-569e-886c-80bc60ca20d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{x,y\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494866} :answer-field/id #uuid "14dab3b2-22c1-5f2b-adcf-90441344d58c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c03ab7a-4491-5a50-9d10-a9d4303200d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105127" :question/problem "If $X=\\{x,y\\},$ then $P(X)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](images/be/bea8536b726a48046b995d180bd9136146d491721a9197f696c7a5e9af43a6ba.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{x\\},\\,\\{y\\},\\,\\{x,y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)=\\{∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{x,y\\}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371485 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e22a7b0-753b-51b1-8946-5d17456aa778" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f87ce3ea-2e44-566e-9046-42997d83dec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371487} {:answer/id #uuid "2e79ece2-46b0-5248-ada9-8809e4f1dc84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371488} {:answer/id #uuid "d948b64d-82a1-5417-9ca3-74c3bb7db176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371489} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c87382-1036-5603-a5d9-8e82172c1e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371490} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f8d4c1-e0b3-5770-a66a-4dafee82cadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d948b64d-82a1-5417-9ca3-74c3bb7db176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371489} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e2617a4-d46c-5b9f-91af-14610bdb6ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32b58d47-77da-59a3-a1da-88971d941837" :question/math-academy-id "q-105137" :question/problem "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are sets. If $|X|=2$ and $|Y|=6,$ then $|P(X)|+|P(Y)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S$, $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|X|=2$ and $|Y|=6,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(X)|+|P(Y)| & ={2}^{|X|}+{2}^{|Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{2}^{6} \\\\  & =4+64 \\\\  & =68.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e22a7b0-753b-51b1-8946-5d17456aa778" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bb5be5a-25fc-5243-a0a7-d419679e5c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494538} {:answer/id #uuid "b880071f-cd23-5321-bef1-28e108f31adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494750} {:answer/id #uuid "d1249453-5a0e-5a14-93c6-359ff868f213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494816} {:answer/id #uuid "e94edc0d-f8b1-5079-90dc-7efac6603889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494871} {:answer/id #uuid "f29511ba-7f18-5c45-958f-b93413c35ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b880071f-cd23-5321-bef1-28e108f31adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494750} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f7ab2b3-fc07-54ae-97c0-4588ea2f4b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7e6e44c-b5ac-5425-8892-5340b5b344d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105149" :question/problem "If $K=\\{3,k,9\\},$ then $|P(K)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $K,$ we have $|P(K)|={2}^{|K|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|K|=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n|P(K)|={2}^{|K|}={2}^{3}=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d82cc69-03ca-5471-acc1-9da617683063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051225} {:answer/id #uuid "9feea6eb-19f7-556e-a7d4-b2886b796fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051226} {:answer/id #uuid "caa29fd2-036b-5b30-96a3-1cbbd9faf312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051227} {:answer/id #uuid "e41ae800-452b-5b16-9c41-afd50e8099c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051228} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2bf2aa-e983-5923-9372-c7185ed7ee8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d82cc69-03ca-5471-acc1-9da617683063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051225} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b13b447-85d3-5825-82c9-3a957f5e3596" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ff27f61-1c9a-545a-9185-30e18e60d035" :question/math-academy-id "q-105150" :question/problem "If $A=\\{2,3\\}$ and $B=∅$ then $|P(A\\times P(B))|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|A|=2,\\,|B|=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n|P(B)|={2}^{|B|}={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A\\times P(B))| & ={2}^{|A\\times P(B)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|A|\\,\\cdot \\,P(B)} \\\\  & ={2}^{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e22a7b0-753b-51b1-8946-5d17456aa778" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3170fd0-b928-5c71-8248-e665229c8b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051405} {:answer/id #uuid "1e139ddb-79ee-549c-958f-10deedc1f08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051406} {:answer/id #uuid "28be5aed-30cb-5437-b05e-0f4d5b777db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051407} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2c8475-cc8c-5e20-95ca-638d3bf9af3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051408} {:answer/id #uuid "54dd0f02-d31e-56fd-b0a3-905c809a0b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54dd0f02-d31e-56fd-b0a3-905c809a0b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051409} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ca4c639-79ac-5bf1-ae75-5363772457b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "609807a5-fc69-5b9b-8c4b-4d835e4fe8a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-1195" :question/problem "Suppose that $A$ is a set. If $|A|=5$, then $|P(A)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $A,$ we have $|P(A)|={2}^{|A|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|A|=5,$ so we have\n\n$$\n|P(A)|={2}^{|A|}={2}^{5}=32.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e5e3846-4681-50a3-9773-00a804ac8630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494375} {:answer/id #uuid "20acfa57-ba3c-50b2-bb9e-5983c1d52588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494381} {:answer/id #uuid "8affc093-0d42-5251-829d-298db802893d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494633} {:answer/id #uuid "df9ade01-7caa-541b-8ee0-1d15f0996bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,2,4,8,\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494847} {:answer/id #uuid "eb79cdae-6d66-5016-97e5-c17676e59ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{2,4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20acfa57-ba3c-50b2-bb9e-5983c1d52588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494381} :answer-field/id #uuid "595f6f8e-2567-512e-a222-db6ad6900a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "350a2acf-787e-5ee2-949f-2438ca3d2b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1203" :question/problem "If $X=\\{2,4,8\\}$, then $P(X)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](images/58/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{2\\},\\,\\{4\\},\\,\\{8\\},\\,\\{2,4\\},\\,\\{2,8\\},\\,\\{4,8\\},\\,\\{2,4,8\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)=\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c1c389c-dbb1-53dc-ac4d-4e01a9c976c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{∅\\},\\{0\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494343} {:answer/id #uuid "b94a6e8e-3cef-5f35-b5b6-00983e01cf9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494751} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe3119c-b864-5462-9e05-10fa108548dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{0\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494838} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b1c88c-f1cb-5698-bf02-cd8fe3fdcdd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494872} {:answer/id #uuid "fd19a9b6-5134-5a6d-9dea-f118fbddcbc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbe3119c-b864-5462-9e05-10fa108548dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{0\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494838} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8af6849-bbbd-5257-abdf-809ae009ea35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7946c285-f988-5068-b516-3298112d9fdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-1204" :question/problem "If $Y=\\{0\\}$, then $P(Y)=$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $Y,$ denoted $P(Y),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $Y,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list out the subsets of $Y:$\n\n- The subset with no elements is $∅.$\n\n- The subset with $1$ element is $Y$ itself: $\\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y)=\\{∅,\\{0\\}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd097735-fa55-589d-9594-34bdbd607a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,536" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372393} {:answer/id #uuid "3a46b546-0817-517d-ae23-82a6eae47732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372394} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0e2f07-9331-5d38-9395-f8fc67c1c11e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,024" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372395} {:answer/id #uuid "6921ab35-c60f-5f43-9eba-0889e5f87645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372396} {:answer/id #uuid "d28a898e-a62b-5210-bada-7d9a8db4dc32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd097735-fa55-589d-9594-34bdbd607a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,536" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372393} :answer-field/id #uuid "8713ad7c-37d7-5134-a2cb-fa0ff4713712" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23139fd9-d255-51c7-b39b-28cddd3cf6e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182215" :question/problem "If $|B|=2$ then $|P(P(P(B)))|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|B|=2.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(B)|={2}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(B))| & ={2}^{|P(B)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(B)))| & ={2}^{|P(P(B))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{16} \\\\  & =65\\,536.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bafffb-5f0c-5c61-9e90-3d17123e83b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383675} {:answer/id #uuid "052967b6-fb43-5e95-a31e-43b0b94be836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383676} {:answer/id #uuid "55b8265d-0309-53c7-9240-42c3bc5039a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383677} {:answer/id #uuid "8196ea70-1091-54e2-b900-6d0e1a1e1d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383678} {:answer/id #uuid "f748cce5-3e62-5bf7-9d93-1c282e88d229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8196ea70-1091-54e2-b900-6d0e1a1e1d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383678} :answer-field/id #uuid "148bd5bb-a19e-5aa5-8d46-0156bb7a5c5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17503d54-27f5-530c-9f6d-5a30b7aa466b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182218" :question/problem "If $|X|=0$ then $|P(P(P(X)))|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S$, we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $|X|=0.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n|P(X)|={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(X)))| & ={2}^{|P(X))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(P(X))| & ={2}^{|P(P(X)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36059e63-9c7a-5044-a5ff-3b7c78c5dfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494429} {:answer/id #uuid "4794f642-3b02-51ca-9585-9769bde5fecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494461} {:answer/id #uuid "680911ea-bae1-58de-a47e-87ff2e8dfc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494525} {:answer/id #uuid "72e7fe21-cd04-5a89-bcbe-229db8147b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494565} {:answer/id #uuid "7734f6e2-fb37-506c-9eb4-4527bf88dc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72e7fe21-cd04-5a89-bcbe-229db8147b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494565} :answer-field/id #uuid "0897cc65-9984-54a2-806e-46d5a90e4e82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae77173a-2ca2-505c-a9f6-aa510463577a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182220" :question/problem "If $A=\\{a,b\\}$ and $B=\\{-1,0,1\\}$ then $|P(A)\\times P(B)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|A|=2,\\,|B|=3.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A)| & ={2}^{|A|}={2}^{2}=4, \\\\ |P(B)| & ={2}^{|B|}={2}^{3}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A)\\times P(B)| & =|P(A)|\\cdot |P(B)| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ec1dc0-4e21-5001-959e-ed35039ca00e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cardinality in More Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa2c4ff-0153-57ef-b2da-d7857daa6674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372407} {:answer/id #uuid "0738be5e-320c-53d1-b477-85f540ec0e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372408} {:answer/id #uuid "213da24e-3ba3-56e1-8f70-a2a77cb72023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372409} {:answer/id #uuid "66674441-1c75-53d9-86ed-276306c7f760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372410} {:answer/id #uuid "8542c241-c995-5fef-bed2-cf1e26117a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0738be5e-320c-53d1-b477-85f540ec0e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372408} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c64fa3-c4a7-55bf-986b-6474978ea29c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a57e2ec-6280-5dcd-8f47-bb36c3489753" :question/math-academy-id "q-182223" :question/problem "If $Y=\\{1\\}$ and $Z=\\{m,n\\}$ then $|P(Z)\\times P(Y\\times Z)|=$" :question/worked-solution "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|Y|=1,\\,|Z|=2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Y\\times Z)| & ={2}^{|Y\\times Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|Y|\\,\\cdot \\,|Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1\\cdot 2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Z)\\times P(Y\\times Z)| & =|P(Z)|\\cdot |P(Y\\times Z)| \\\\  & ={2}^{|Z|}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.