answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd9eceba-08ff-5052-86b4-313736cb0156" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a540711c-ecf6-55f0-99c0-da5fdfa24e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-182224" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$\n- **III.** $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be ${∅}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{a},{∅},{a,∅}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${∅}$ is ${∅,{∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19828ad7-6154-5b2d-840b-b3b96f511f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494368} {:answer/id #uuid "60b488d3-4af9-5408-86d2-64b7a88c37f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494517} {:answer/id #uuid "c1edf78e-6f48-5a04-a34c-815cb29263ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494774} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd790ba-34d4-55f8-967b-992968640c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494801} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b76802-f72d-59b0-b07c-30e15c9a52bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1edf78e-6f48-5a04-a34c-815cb29263ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494774} :answer-field/id #uuid "40cf1680-4aee-5c33-aa84-ca0ab1d7eb28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c09d0cf0-247f-5da8-86ac-5074f5239c65" :question/math-academy-id "q-182230" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(∅)=\\{∅\\}$\n\nII. $P(a)=\\{∅,\\{a\\}\\}$\n\nIII. $P(\\{∅,\\{∅\\}\\})=\\{∅,\\{∅,\\{∅\\}\\}\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the power set of the set $∅$ is $\\{∅\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $a$ is not a set. So, the notation $P(a)$ does not make sense.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that we are given the set $\\{∅,\\{∅\\}\\}.$ So, its power set must be $\\{∅,\\{∅\\},\\{\\{∅\\}\\},\\{∅,\\{∅\\}\\}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answe