ifficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c6c0e2c1-4d3b-51cf-9630-3617d7834c7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-182242" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the power set of the set $∅$ is ${∅}.$ Therefore, $P(P(∅))={∅,{∅}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{∅}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({∅}))={∅,{∅},{{∅}},{∅,{∅}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that we are given the set ${0}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{0}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({0}))={∅,{∅},{{0}},{∅,{0}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} {:answer/id #uuid "34298241-b946-5a36-9d6f-cdccc915da9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a45469e-136a-5e5b-b99c-d0986cc05aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471209} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5ec5c4-62cb-56d9-bab7-8189327c57a5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bc87f60-846a-5297-91f2-4b0d573ccaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471211} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2c37cf-9e89-5f2f-836e-fe89e922b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471212} :answer-field/id #uuid "7348f3ad-5c47-51b6-adc0-96ac7ad27556" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} {:answer/id #uuid "c008f84e-6f4f-5a9b-bf98-a8afad9a4478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e69bd74-d6db-5f41-aaba-1646f9178cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471213} :answer-field/id #uuid "68fd73fa-c23e-5720-9d17-1ef1a6a7e99e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afe01a46-709c-5c6f-b721-547dd77ac300" :question/math-academy-id "q-182244" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P(P(2))={∅,{2}}$\n- **II.** $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}$\n- **III.** $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{{2}}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that $2$ is not a set. So, the notation $P(P(2))$ does not make sense.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that we are given the set ${2}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{2}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({2}))={∅,{∅},{{2}},{∅,{2}}}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that we are given the set ${{2}}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{{2}}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({{2}}))={∅,{∅},{{{2}}},{∅,{{2}}}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f1f99d3-ebcb-50c6-a162-bd58f7d5ec92" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Elements in a Power Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172f8ad4-9f1b-5676-8d3f-54267405333f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{4\\},\\{\\{∅\\}\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494365} {:answer/id #uuid "322ae03d-133c-5074-9e05-af54ba584511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{4\\},\\{\\{∅\\}\\},\\{4,\\{∅\\}\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494417} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed5500f-bcf2-53ee-834e-61226994af42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{4\\},\\{\\{∅\\}\\},\\{4,\\{∅\\}\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494554} {:answer/id #uuid "9a801ce9-232f-5884-9a02-c3c2fe9c87d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{4\\},\\{∅\\},\\{\\{4\\},\\{∅\\}\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494671} {:answer/id #uuid "dceabe73-fed2-5041-8609-f752f3b509e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860